      "text": "I fixed the places where the code departed from SPEC.md, and the five public tests still pass. I didn't write new tests for the fixes, so they are only checked against the tests that were already there.\n\n- **Receiving:** stock received into an existing lot id now adds to its quantity instead of replacing it (`src/inventory.ts`).\n- **Available stock:** expired lots no longer count towards a sku's available stock (`src/inventory.ts`).\n- **Lot order:** lots with the same expiry are now used in ascending id order, where they were descending before (`src/inventory.ts`).\n- **Repeated skus:** order lines with the same sku are added together before reserving (`src/orders.ts`).\n- **All or nothing:** when a line can't be filled, everything the order had already reserved is released. Before, only the first line's reservation was released (`src/orders.ts`).\n- **Cancelled orders:** they are dropped from the backorder queue on retry and never reserved again (`src/backorder.ts`).\n- **Shipping:** the limit is now the units still reserved for that sku, not the original line quantity (`src/warehouse.ts`).\n- **Cancelling:** it releases only the units still reserved, so shipped units stay shipped (`src/warehouse.ts`).\n- **Returns:** a returned unit is restocked if its lot is still usable that day, meaning its expiry is on or after that day. The old check let it in a day late (`src/warehouse.ts`).\n\nI left the snapshot shape as it was.",
